# MCsquare validation

`cargo test` covers the GPU Monte Carlo with self-checking unit tests. Agreement with MCsquare lives in `validation/` and is deliberately outside `cargo test` — it needs the `third_party/MCsquare` submodule and a GPU.

- Only run it after changing Monte Carlo physics or transport: `mc_transport.wgsl`, `mc.rs`, `mc_materials.npz` (`cargo run -p scan-kit-io --bin build-mc-tables`), the CT calibration (`calibration.rs`), or the beam model (`beam.rs`). UI, catalog, or other dose-view changes don't need it. The slab suites and the patient suite both check the Rust engine the app runs. The patient suite also checks dose-weighted LETd.
- `cargo run -p scan-kit-compute --bin mc-validate -- fast` (about 30 s) after each physics change; `cargo run -p scan-kit-compute --bin mc-validate -- full` (about 10 min) before a PR with physics changes.
- `cargo run -p scan-kit-compute --bin mc-validate -- patient` (about 1 min) after changing voxel transport, the CT calibration, or the beam model.
- Don't pass `--write-goldens` unless the user asks. It reruns MCsquare (needs `MCSQUARE_DIR` pointing at a build with a runnable binary, many minutes) and is only needed when a case in `cases.rs` changes or MCsquare is updated.
